.push([1,\"25:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"5\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"This ancient pilgrimage site is one of the five panchtirthis of Jaisalmer. The principal miraculous deity of this place remains present even today, and many fortunate devotees have the experience of seeing Dharanendra Dev. Four small temples stand at the four corners of the main temple, housing the images of Adinath, Ajitnath, Sambhavnath, and Chintamani Parshwanath. Since this temple is located at Lodrava, it is also known as \\\\\\\"Lodrava Parshwanath.\\\\\\\" This Parshwanath is also known as \\\\\\\"Chintamani Parshwanath.\\\\\\\" This temple was renovated in Vikram Samvat 2034. This image of Lodrava Parshwanath is striking, magnificent, and miraculous, and many miracles continue to occur here. The six-foot form of Dharanendra Dev has been seen here many times, and many pilgrims have had this vision. During the India-Pakistan war, while bombing was taking place throughout the conflict, Dharanendra Dev was seen walking on the spire of the temple, protecting it. Many people witnessed this event.\\\"}]\\n26:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"6\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Other Temples: There are no other temples, but there is a Dadawadi.\\\"}]\\n27:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"7\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Art and Sculpture: It is difficult to find elsewhere an image as miraculous and artistic as this image of Lord Sahastraphana Parshwanath. Every pillar, ceiling, and spire presents a vivid display of skilled craftsmanship. This temple, built by Dhirushah, is a beautiful example of masterful artistry. Looking at the images here, everyone feels that the sculptors were engaged in an eager competition to achieve dazzling beauty. The artistry of the main arched gateway is truly beautiful. The carvings of the Samavasaran, Ashtapadgiri, and the kalpavriksha are exquisite and well worth seeing. The ancient wooden chariot, too, is beautifully carved and worth seeing.\\\"}]\\n28:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"8\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Directions: Jaisalmer railway station is 15 kilometers from here. Bus services and private vehicles are available here. Dharmashala and bhojanshala facilities are available, along with an upashraya.\\\"}]\\n29:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"9\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Scripture References: This temple is mentioned in the \\\\\\\"Shatdal Padmayantra\\\\\\\" and the \\\\\\\"Lodrapuri Chintamani Parshwanath Stavan.\\\\\\\" An image of Lodrava Parshwanath is also found at Jiravala Tirth and Bhildiyaji Tirth. There is a temple of Lodrava Parshwanath at Vepery in Chennai.\\\"}]\\n2a:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"10\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Praise (Stuti): You stand guard over this land's borders, protecting the entire country; upon your head rest the serpent hoods, and your name is Lodrava, where devotees come ceaselessly, day and night, to meet the Lord with the devotion of the serpent-king. \\\\\\\"With devotion I bow to Shri Lodrava Parshwa.\\\\\\\"\\\"}]\\n2b:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"11\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Chanting Mantra: \\\\\\\"Om Hrim Arham Shri Lodrava Parshwanathaya Namah.\\\\\\\"\\\"}]\\n2c:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"12\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Trust: Shri Jaisalmer Lodrapur Parshwanath Jain Shwetambar Trust, Post: Lodrapur, Via Jaisalmer, District: Jaisalmer - 345001, Rajasthan. Phone: 02992-50165, Mobile: 9460373142.\\\"}]\\n\"])</script></body></html>","rscData":"","segmentData":{"/_tree":"","/_full":"","/$d$lang/tirtha/$d$slug/__PAGE__":"","/$d$lang/tirtha/$d$slug":"","/$d$lang/tirtha":"","/$d$lang":"","/_index":"","/_head":""},"headers":{"x-nextjs-stale-time":"300","x-nextjs-prerender":"1","x-next-cache-tags":"_N_T_/layout,_N_T_/[lang]/layout,_N_T_/[lang]/tirtha/layout,_N_T_/[lang]/tirtha/[slug]/layout,_N_T_/[lang]/tirtha/[slug]/page,_N_T_/en/tirtha/tirtha-085"},"segmentPaths":["/_tree","/_full","/$d$lang/tirtha/$d$slug/__PAGE__","/$d$lang/tirtha/$d$slug","/$d$lang/tirtha","/$d$lang","/_index","/_head"],"revalidate":60,"cacheControl":{"revalidate":60,"ex